{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p1-34327fa9","text":"The user asked to run the server locally, open /reports/custom/add, generate a report with the AI assistant, and verify the «listo» event arrives with the preview. This needs: starting the server, logging in, having an AI provider/agent configured, and performing a real AI run — which requires a real API key/provider. Since no provider credentials exist, the AI call would fail. I'll start the server, verify the page loads, and test what I can (perhaps the stream mechanism end-to-end without real AI — e.g., instrument with a fake provider if tests support that, or at least confirm the stream isn't dead by triggering the endpoint and seeing the SSE progress events).

Let me start by checking how to run the server (cmd/server), config (configs/config.go), env, DB. Then start the server in background, register preview, open /reports/custom/add, log in... need credentials. Maybe there's a default admin or a way to log in in dev. Check first_run / login defaults. Also check AI provider configuration — without an active provider, aiRunLoop errors "no hay proveedor de IA activo con API key". But the stream should still deliver progress (Fase 1 attempt) and the error event over SSE — which actually verifies the delivery fix (events reach the browser!). Then, if we can configure a fake provider pointed at a test server, we could see a real "listo".

Given the scope: do it honestly. Step 1: inspect config/env. Let me check .env, config defaults, and how tests seed providers. There's ai_respan_test.go with proveedorDePrueba. There may be an env var for AI provider (aiRespanAPIKeyEnv) — when empty, "sin proveedor activo". 

Plan:
1. Build & start server (check .env in workspace).
2. Login with default credentials (check seed - maybe admin/admin123 in seed SQL).
3. Open browser, login, go to /reports/custom/add, open the modal, type a report request, click Generar.
4. Observe: progress events arrive in the console (previously only first event arrived) — this directly validates the gzip passthrough fix. Even if the AI call fails due to no provider, the STREAM will show multiple progress + error event, i.e., the delivery works end-to-end.
5. Optionally configure a local fake OpenAI provider to get a full «listo». That requires inserting a provider row via the UI (Configuración IA). There may be a screen to create provider with vendor "openai-compatible" pointing to a URL. If feasible, spin a fake provider server and add it via the UI. That would produce a real informe + preview + listo event. That's the gold standard.

Let me explore.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"}
